          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.087,
            0.847,
            0.109
          ],
          "content": "In general, **if A is divisible by k, then all multiples of A are divisible by k.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.109,
            0.848,
            0.151
          ],
          "content": "？ 4. If a number is divisible by 12, then the number is also divisible by all the factors of 12."
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.088,
            0.156,
            0.904,
            0.41
          ],
          "content": "<table><tr><td colspan=3>Explanation with Algebra and Visualisation</td><td>Examples</td></tr><tr><td>A number divisible by12 is a multiple of 12.</td><td>12m</td><td></td><td>12, 24, 36, 48,108, 132.</td></tr><tr><td>Factors of multiples of12 will include factorsof 12.</td><td>12m $= 2 \\times 6 \\times m$  $= 3 \\times 4 \\times m$ </td><td><img src=\"images/page_8_table_image_3_1.jpg\"/>A factor of 12 covers a row fully.Hence, it covers all multiples of 12fully.</td><td>Factors of 24: 1,2, 3, 4, 6, 8, 12,24.</td></tr></table>",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_8_table_3.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.424,
            0.848,
            0.464
          ],
          "content": "In general, **if A is divisible by k, then A is divisible by all the factors of k.** Hence, Statement 4 is always true."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.109,
            0.469,
            0.847,
            0.51
          ],
          "content": "？ 5. If a number is divisible by 7, then it is also divisible by any multiple of 7."
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.087,
