            0.849
          ],
          "content": "<table><tr><td colspan=4>Explanation with Algebra and Visualisation</td><td>Examples</td></tr><tr><td>Numbers divisible by7 are multiples of 7.</td><td>7k</td><td></td><td><img src=\"images/page_8_table_image_6_1.jpg\"/></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Multiples of 7.7k will be divisible by7m if and only if m is afactor of k.</td><td colspan=3>个7m $Ifk = ym$                  <img src=\"images/page_8_table_image_6_2.jpg\"/>then $7k \\div 7m =$                                  k rows $\\mathit { 7 y m } \\div 7 m$ <img src=\"images/page_8_table_image_6_3.jpg\"/></td><td>42 $( 7 \\times 6 )$ is divisibleby 7 but it is notdivisible by $2 8 \\: ( 7 \\times 4 )$ 42 $( 7 \\times 6 )$ is divisibleby 7 and it is divisibleby $1 4 \\left( 7 \\times 2 \\right)$ </td></tr></table>",
